WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Tesla's software update fixed cyber truck door rattle without a recall or service visit. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 609. Tesla received confirmation for an order of 5,000 optimus units. A factory audit is scheduled next. The order represents the first large external commitment for the humanoid platform. Chinese robotics shares increased after reports that Tesla started an audit of its optimus program. The review proceeds a potential 5,000 units.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.140
5000-unit robot order. While the robot's side-eye volume production, Tesla's energy storage

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:42.660
business is already executing at scale in Europe. Work began on a 2.8-gigawatt-hour battery

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:49.040
storage project using Tesla Equipment. The project pairs Tesla MegaPak units with local renewable

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.720
generation. Site preparation includes foundation work and electrical interconnection planning.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.860
The Limondale Project marks Australia's first large-scale megapack deployment.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.940
Deployment uses pre-assembled units to accelerate commissioning.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:08.120
The system integrates with existing grid infrastructure in new South Wales.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:14.740
Battery storage projects now anchor grid planning in markets that once treated them as optional add-ons.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:20.900
A 2.8-gigawatt-hour installation in Belgium illustrates how utilities size these systems

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:24.920
to match renewable output curves rather than peak demand alone.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.620
Tesla's Megapack deployments follow the same logic at larger scale.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.400
Each unit ships pre-configured for rapid interconnection,

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.060
which reduces on-site labor and shortens the time between contract and revenue.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:42.120
When storage economics improve faster than transmission permitting,

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.360
the lowest cost path through reliability moves from wires to batteries.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:54.220
Tesla's role in that shift rests on repeatable factory output and standardized software rather than bespoke site engineering.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.600
Tesla resolved a hardware issue through an over-the-air software update.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.660
The fix eliminates the need for physical service on affected vehicles.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.500
Owners can apply the change remotely without scheduling time at a service center.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:12.420
The approach demonstrates how software can address mechanical concerns after delivery.

